  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 205 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nGuidance consensus is that the upper-level flow over the Middle \nMississippi will remain generally northwesterly through the extended \nforecast period. Despite this, low-level ridging centered over the \nregion will continue feeding warm air into the region, supporting \nabove normal surface temperatures through the first portion of the \nweek. \n\nStarting Wednesday and continuing through the end of the workweek, \nan upper-level trough will deepen over the eastern CONUS and send a \nseries of shortwaves through the Midwest. This phasing of the upper \nlevels supports flow through the depth of the atmosphere becoming \nnorth-northwesterly. Despite both deterministic guidance and \nensemble clusters favoring this solution, how the trough and \nsubsequent shortwaves evolve varies among guidance sources. This \nwill dictate the placement of a cooler, more seasonable air mass as \nit moves across the eastern CONUS through the latter portion of the \nworkweek. A more glancing blow, which is currently favored by a \nmajority of guidance and the NBM, will gradually cool temperatures \nthrough the period to around climatological normals. A more direct \nhit from the air mass would lead to daily highs struggling to break \n50 degrees by Friday per cooler ensemble members. With the CWA \nexpected to be on the periphery of this air mass, I do expect our \ntemperature forecast for this portion of the period to fluctuate in \nthe coming days as guidance hones in on a common solution. \n\nAs for precipitation chances, a lack of notable return flow from the \nGulf through the period and dry antecedent conditions lead to low \nconfidence in precipitation chances, including toward the end of the \nweek when the upper-level trough deepens over the eastern CONUS. \nDepending on the potency and track of embedded shortwaves, there is \na very low chance (10%) for light rainfall roughly on Friday. \nSubsequent waves would have less moisture to work with, leading to \neven lower chances as we move into next weekend.",
